{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 2981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's perfectly obvious the time has a direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2974,
    "dDurationMs": 4032,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All we mean by that is that the past is different from the future\nin lots of different ways"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7035,
    "dDurationMs": 2979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We were younger in the past,\nwe will be older in the future"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10020,
    "dDurationMs": 2896,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We remember the past,\nwe don't remember the future"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12939,
    "dDurationMs": 3178,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The surprise is that that difference\nbetween past and future"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16110,
    "dDurationMs": 3415,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is nowhere to be found\nin the deep down laws of physics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19525,
    "dDurationMs": 4336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Time is actually a lot like space\nif you're out in a space suit flying around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23854,
    "dDurationMs": 2454,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there will be no difference \nbetween up, down, left, right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26340,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "likewise, there is no intrinsic difference\nbetween the past and the future"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30944,
    "dDurationMs": 3304,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the laws of physics.\nNow that's not completely a mystery to us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34279,
    "dDurationMs": 2150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we know that what actually happens\nin the real world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36461,
    "dDurationMs": 2449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that you're not just made of \none or two particles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38903,
    "dDurationMs": 3163,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bumping into each other,\nyou're a very very complicated collection"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42075,
    "dDurationMs": 4308,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of many many particles and\nthey're becoming more disorderly with time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46381,
    "dDurationMs": 3157,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is just saying that entropy increases."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49552,
    "dDurationMs": 3342,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The interesting thing is that every\ndifference between the past and the future"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52896,
    "dDurationMs": 4009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will utimately be traced to the fact that\nthe entropy was lower"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56907,
    "dDurationMs": 3316,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the past and is growing.\nThat's the Second Law of Thermodynamics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60210,
    "dDurationMs": 3251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The universe was orderly,\nit's becoming more disorderly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63456,
    "dDurationMs": 4584,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's not a surprise. There is more ways\nto be disorderly than to be orderly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68054,
    "dDurationMs": 4387,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The suprise is that the universe was ever\nlow entropy to begin with."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72441,
    "dDurationMs": 4991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we go all the way back to the Big Bang,\n13.7 billion years ago, the universe began"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77435,
    "dDurationMs": 4264,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a highly ordered state. So, modern\ncosmologists are trying to understand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81699,
    "dDurationMs": 4098,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right now why the early universe was in\na such precise state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85804,
    "dDurationMs": 3693,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why it was so low entropy.\nOnce we understand that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89492,
    "dDurationMs": 2950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it will make perfect sense to us\nwhy the arrow of time stretches"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92450,
    "dDurationMs": 5945,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as it does from the past to today\nall the way toward the future."
    } ]
  } ]
}
